-- SWEEP-PROBE-FIXES-B-1 (2026-10-26, charter pillars autonomy and cost; agent_issues 1000198, 1000243, 1000285, 1000155), probe and trigger calibration bundle B.
-- Follows migrations/2026-10-26-chaos-drill-calibration.sql: a disabled '<name>@before-calibration-1' history row keeps each old probe, each edit is guarded so a second apply, or a probe someone has
-- since changed, is left alone, and the Rollback line restores everything it changed. Re-measured at 2026-10-26T09:20Z (qnfo-audit, SELECT only) before any row was written.
--   1. remediation reopen on relapse (spof_alternate_probes, issue 1000198): the probe demands a recurrence_guard_actions row in 7 days. The table has 0 rows in 7 days (465 in all, the last
--      2026-10-18T11:04:07Z) because no closure has relapsed since, while the D1 path is armed (trigger recurrence_guard_tick present, queue_sla_autofix not off, fleet_tick inserts in minutes
--      0 to 9 from two producers, no closed issue past max_attempts). The old window note admits it: the drill does not manufacture a relapse. It now reads the control, structure first, so
--      an old action row no longer excuses a trigger that is gone (precedent CHAOS-DRILL-TICK-ALT-1), and the trigger's own relapse select is part of it with a 75 minute settle so the hour
--      between two gate windows does not read as a failure.
--   2. agent-ws-reactivation-prerequisites (control_alternate_probes, issue 1000243): the probe requires the code-task line in the description of issue 1000140. qnfo-code-orchestrator
--      NEEDS-ANCHOR-ROUTE-1 rewrote it to session-task at 2026-10-25T18:53Z, 52 minutes after the last pass, because no code task can place an edit in the 2.4 MB bundle and the work waits on
--      the fleet cap (36 workers on 2026-10-26, cap 30). The handoff the alternate_path names is the issue and its CI-applied contract (issue-1000140: active, runner-https, min_version 2.1.0), and that
--      contract is intact, so the probe reads the contract instead of a line a loop rewrites.
--   3. compat-advance-review-gate (control_alternate_probes, issue 1000285): the probe demands an ok compat-verify event in 7 days. The verifier writes one only when a reviewed compatibility
--      date advances (3 events ever: 2026-10-13, 10-18, 10-19) and nothing waits to advance (GET /compat: 33 workers declare their live date, 2 declare none, workers_compat_date_behind 0),
--      so the probe measured a rare event as a 7 day rate. It now fails on a pending advance left unsettled for 2 hours, a stale exposure snapshot, or an advance that waits with no
--      verification in 35 days.
--   4. v_cost_forecast (issue 1000155, critical): migration_runs 518 (2026-10-24T09:45:39Z) applied migrations/2026-10-21-cost-sustain-forecast.sql again after migration_runs 515 had created
--      the bounded view, and its DROP VIEW / CREATE VIEW replaced the 15-column view by the 11-column COST-SUSTAIN-1 one. scripts/cost_ledger.py write_forecast skips the bound when the
--      column is missing, so fleet_cost_bound_month_usd stayed at 352.76 (2026-10-25T08:45:00Z) for over a day while the pace and forecast metrics refreshed, and the dashboard cost feed lost
--      fleet_bound_30d_usd. This file backs the view up, recreates the bounded view (the text of the COST-SUSTAIN-3 migration, the first 11 columns unchanged and in order, readers: scripts/
--      cost_ledger.py and the dashboard cost feed, both SELECT *), writes the metric from it, and registers a failure mode with a detector. Read from the restored view at 09:20Z the bound is
--      USD 329.21 per 30 days (852,612 neurons a day), over the owner budget of 300, so the largest-cap lever the trigger names is applied: research_daily_neurons 360000 to 310000 and
--      q08_daily_neurons 150000 to 100000 (50k neurons a day each, USD 296.2). The 7 day uncapped remainder carries two qnfo-ops days of 274k and 205k neurons (2026-10-24, 10-25, against 2k to 15k
--      on other days) that leave the window on 2026-11-02, so the trim also keeps the bound from flapping around 300 on one stray day. Both caps are pacing budgets: work over the pace waits, no gate changes.
--   Not applied, premise gone: issues 1000217 and 1000234 (operator '>' read as >=). BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 (migrations/2026-10-26-breach-one-meaning.sql, PR 4444) already rewrote
--   v_metric_trigger_state to read the symbols, set the five rows to 'gt' and added the triggers metric_trigger_operator_words_ai and _au; v_metric_trigger_state now reads hit 0 for triggers 14018 and 14085.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
